      "text": "Given that when an integer \\( n \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7, we can express this relationship mathematically as:\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5, and then determine their sum.\n\nFirst, consider the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3. We substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression:\n\\[ n \\equiv 15k + 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\nSince \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 3, it has a remainder of 0 when divided by 3:\n\\[ 15k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\]\nThus,\n\\[ n \\equiv 0 + 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\nTo find the remainder when 7 is divided by 3, we perform the division:\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, consider the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. We substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression:\n\\[ n \\equiv 15k + 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 5, it has a remainder of 0 when divided by 5:\n\\[ 15k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThus,\n\\[ n \\equiv 0 + 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\nTo find the remainder when 7 is divided by 5, we perform the division:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nFinally, we find the sum of the remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
