      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that when an integer \\( x \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7, we can express this relationship as:\n\\[ x = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. Let's start with the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3. We substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into the division:\n\\[ x \\div 3 = 15k + 7 \\div 3 = 15k + 7 - 3 \\cdot 5k = 7 - 15k \\]\nThis shows that the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. Let's calculate that:\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's find the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5. We substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into the division:\n\\[ x \\div 5 = 15k + 7 \\div 5 = 15k + 7 - 5k = 5k + 7 \\]\nThis shows that the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. Let's calculate that:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of these remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
