      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that an integer \\( x \\) when divided by 15 leaves a remainder of 7, we can express this relationship as:\n\\[ x = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 and by 5 and then sum these remainders.\n\nFirst, consider the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3. We substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into this division:\n\\[ x \\div 3 = (15k + 7) \\div 3 = 5k + \\frac{7}{3} \\]\nSince \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 3, it does not affect the remainder when divided by 3. Thus, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. We calculate:\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, consider the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5. We substitute \\( x = 15k + 7 \\) into this division:\n\\[ x \\div 5 = (15k + 7) \\div 5 = 3k + \\frac{7}{5} \\]\nSince \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 5, it does not affect the remainder when divided by 5. Thus, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. We calculate:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we sum the remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
